From af97b2079cb6809018fd856061770fa186f3282c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: avdim <avdimdv@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:31:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] swcodec apex: let sphal fall back to /system/lib on
 non-VNDK devices

On a vndk-lite device (ro.vndk.lite=true, no BOARD_VNDK_VERSION) there is
no /system/lib/vndk-sp-29, so media.swcodec could not dlopen the gralloc
mapper passthrough HAL ("android.hardware.graphics.mapper@2.0.so not
found" from the sphal namespace). C2AllocatorGralloc then had no mapper
and every software video decode with graphic output failed
(C2SoftAvcDec: fetchGraphicBlock failed with status 14).

Visible effect on the Galaxy Alpha: every video thumbnail fell back to
the Exynos OMX hardware decoder, which sometimes deadlocks in freeNode
and then blocks the next MediaRecorder.start() forever.

Search /system/lib last, as the system's legacy linker config does.
Verified on device: c2.android.avc.decoder decodes thumbnails, no
fallback to OMX.Exynos.AVC.Decoder.

Change-Id: I91494d203c72f4658b56ffc061645081c4332f9d
---
 apex/ld.config.txt | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/apex/ld.config.txt b/apex/ld.config.txt
index af8ec066c0..68595beadc 100644
--- a/apex/ld.config.txt
+++ b/apex/ld.config.txt
@@ -131,3 +131,9 @@ namespace.sphal.link.platform.shared_libs = libEGL.so:libGLESv1_CM.so:libGLESv2.
 
 # Add a link for libz.so which is llndk on devices where VNDK is not enforced.
 namespace.sphal.link.platform.shared_libs += libz.so
+
+# Non-VNDK (vndk-lite) devices have no /system/${LIB}/vndk-sp${VNDK_VER}: the VNDK-SP libraries
+# the gralloc mapper passthrough HAL needs (android.hardware.graphics.mapper@2.0.so, libhidlbase, ...)
+# live in plain /system/${LIB}. Fall back to it, as the system's legacy linker config does.
+namespace.sphal.search.paths += /system/${LIB}
+namespace.sphal.permitted.paths += /system/${LIB}
